 \begin{abstract}
-AI workloads mix precisions and shift toward lower precision, so splitting tensor-core peak throughput across 16/8/4-bit floating-point formats becomes a key design choice. DP-Puzzle combines shared multi-precision datapaths with precision-specific compute units to tune throughput allocation; we compare nine configurations, jointly modeling area, power, and precision migration. At 12 nm and 1 GHz, doubling FP4 throughput raises area by 33.6\% while improving area and energy efficiency by 49.7\% and 27.3\%. At matched area and power, 1:2:8 performs best overall among the nine, yielding a modeled 1.13× compute-only speedup on DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash GEMMs. Moderate expansion thus balances low-precision capacity and deployment density.
