 \subsection{Deployment Scale Under Joint Budgets}
-All nine candidates share the core-area budget and DP-array power limit of $1:2:4$ ($\beta=1$). The baseline has 36 cores, each with 256 DPs at 1\,GHz and one request per cycle. We set the baseline array-area fraction to $\alpha=0.327$, referencing the reported 32.7\% Cube-cluster share of AI Core area~\cite{luo2024hifloat8area}, and fix peripheral storage and control area per core. Single-DP area and the maximum measured power across precision modes determine the integer core counts allowed by each budget; the smaller count determines deployment. Multiplying this count by DPs per core and precision-specific DP throughput gives chip-level peak throughput. Deployment remains fixed across workloads.
